1
00:00:16,370 --> 00:00:17,750
Alright.

2
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:19,207
Who do you want to choose?

3
00:00:20,208 --> 00:00:24,080
I still want Kunigami,
that number 50.

4
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,700
As a post player, his standard
of ball protection is very high.

5
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,093
With him, we can get
many opportunities in the front line.

6
00:00:30,093 --> 00:00:33,137
That way, I can score even more goals.

7
00:00:33,137 --> 00:00:37,120
No. In that case, I think Reo
is more suited to be the team's core

8
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,540
and can maintain the balance
in attacking and defending

9
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:41,360
so the three of us can
attack as we please.

10
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:42,855
He's the best choice, isn't he?

11
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:45,410
Yeah, that's true.

12
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:46,450
Right, isn't it?

13
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:49,660
Yes. That really can unite the team.

14
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:52,160
However, if that's the case,

15
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:54,325
this would be a suicidal move
that destroys our chances.

16
00:00:55,576 --> 00:01:00,250
Even though the right action
is to unite the team well,

17
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,916
that's not my style.

18
00:01:01,916 --> 00:01:03,310
Think about it carefully.

19
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:05,044
What's the main key to passing
the second selection?

20
00:01:05,044 --> 00:01:07,046
Chemical reaction, right?

21
00:01:07,046 --> 00:01:09,382
The reason we're here is because
we can create chemical reactions on the field.

22
00:01:09,549 --> 00:01:10,870
We're here because of that.

23
00:01:11,592 --> 00:01:13,410
I devour Barou,

24
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:15,790
and Barou devours me back.

25
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:17,360
We can't predict beforehand

26
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,392
until what stage we can play.

27
00:01:19,392 --> 00:01:21,710
This unpredictable style of play,

28
00:01:21,710 --> 00:01:23,396
that is our soccer.

29
00:01:23,396 --> 00:01:27,870
What I want is someone
who can devour us.

30
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:32,905
If not, we can't defeat them.

31
00:01:32,905 --> 00:01:35,790
Even though this is a gamble,
what you said is absolutely right.

32
00:01:35,790 --> 00:01:39,120
In that case, only that kid fits.

33
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:41,650
Right. In the match,

34
00:01:41,650 --> 00:01:43,875
he was the only striker who
could devour us.

35
00:01:43,875 --> 00:01:47,962
Right. The only one who didn't lose
his own style in this chemical reaction,

36
00:01:47,962 --> 00:01:50,381
it's only you,

37
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:53,343
Hyoma Chigiri.

38
00:01:57,722 --> 00:02:00,933
Come here, we need
your super-fast legs.

39
00:02:08,524 --> 00:02:10,276
Kunigami.

40
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:13,620
Don't forget.

41
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:16,870
We still haven't defeated Isagi.

42
00:02:16,870 --> 00:02:19,160
Remember this same feeling
of unwillingness.

43
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:21,496
I'm waiting for you, Hero.

44
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:28,378
Reo.

45
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:32,250
That last ball,

46
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:35,370
we set a trap because of you.

47
00:02:35,370 --> 00:02:37,637
Your ability is truly incredible.

48
00:02:37,637 --> 00:02:38,888
Your ability is

49
00:02:38,888 --> 00:02:42,850
being able to deliver deceptive passes
in critical moments.

50
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:44,102
Isagi and I believed in your ability,

51
00:02:44,102 --> 00:02:45,770
so we took this big gamble.

52
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:48,290
It was really very dangerous.

53
00:02:48,290 --> 00:02:50,660
You really are incredible.

54
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:53,120
So, I'm going ahead first now.

55
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,028
Then...

56
00:02:54,028 --> 00:02:55,196
In that case, come and take me.

57
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:58,750
I don't need to be consoled.

58
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:00,700
Just say it directly.

59
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:04,370
Say that you no longer need me.

60
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:07,200
You've changed.

61
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:12,580
You've forgotten our promise
to "become number one in the world together."

62
00:03:14,132 --> 00:03:18,500
Damn it. Just throw me away
if that's what you want.

63
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:22,410
I'm asking you.

64
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:25,250
If I choose you, would you feel satisfied?

65
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:27,770
Why? It's not interesting at all

66
00:03:27,770 --> 00:03:30,000
to form a team by relying on
hurt feelings.

67
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,733
Is becoming number one in the world
that easy?

68
00:03:32,733 --> 00:03:36,737
You're the one who forgot our promise.

69
00:03:39,330 --> 00:03:43,200
Fine, whatever you say.

70
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,621
It's really troublesome, Reo.

71
00:03:47,582 --> 00:03:50,293
I don't want to take care of you
anymore.

72
00:03:53,754 --> 00:03:55,540
Reo.

73
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:57,410
Don't just wait to be chosen,

74
00:03:57,410 --> 00:03:59,410
you have to become the person
who has the right to choose.

75
00:03:59,410 --> 00:04:02,250
What are you playing soccer for?

76
00:04:03,830 --> 00:04:06,976
Only the number one striker
in the world

77
00:04:06,976 --> 00:04:09,500
can keep surviving in Blue Lock.

78
00:04:13,733 --> 00:04:16,200
Don't hang your head, look at them closely.

79
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,250
If you still won't accept reality
at a time like this,

80
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,500
then we'll stop right here.

81
00:04:20,990 --> 00:04:25,500
(Rensuke Kunigami, Reo Mikage
Sent Back to the Second Stage)

82
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:28,873
(Yoichi Isagi, Seishiro Nagi
Shouei Barou, Hyoma Chigiri)

83
00:04:28,873 --> 00:04:32,960
(Advance to the Fourth Stage)

84
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:08,014
(Episode 19: The Dancing Boy)

85
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:11,434
An imaginary friend?

86
00:06:11,434 --> 00:06:13,970
Yes. That monster you talk about

87
00:06:13,970 --> 00:06:17,120
must be a friend that
only you can see.

88
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:19,066
Aren't I very weird?

89
00:06:19,066 --> 00:06:20,660
You're not weird.

90
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:24,238
He plays the soccer you want
together with you, doesn't he?

91
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:27,200
But, Mom...

92
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:29,000
I really want

93
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,250
a real friend who can

94
00:06:31,250 --> 00:06:33,122
play soccer happily
with me.

95
00:06:33,122 --> 00:06:36,584
Yes. I hope you can get
a friend like that someday.

96
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:39,330
I'm sure, too.

97
00:06:47,970 --> 00:06:50,540
If Rin is still in the fourth stage,

98
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:52,892
then we can play against him later.

99
00:06:55,770 --> 00:06:58,120
(Fourth Stage, Four-Person Room)
Guys, are you listening to me?

100
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:01,410
Your teammates are discussing
something important.

101
00:07:01,410 --> 00:07:03,040
What's up?

102
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,403
No. It's...

103
00:07:04,403 --> 00:07:06,660
After Nagi and Barou,

104
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:09,330
plus the stubborn Young Lady, Chigiri.

105
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:12,078
It's going to be even more troublesome.

106
00:07:12,078 --> 00:07:13,500
What is this?

107
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:15,910
Whose socks and towel are these?

108
00:07:15,910 --> 00:07:18,292
Socks placed carelessly,
wet towel left lying around.

109
00:07:18,292 --> 00:07:20,580
Those socks are mine.

110
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:23,172
I put them there after drying my hair.
Just leave them.

111
00:07:23,172 --> 00:07:25,080
That towel is mine.

112
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:26,550
Please help me put it in the washing machine.

113
00:07:26,550 --> 00:07:30,513
Put it in yourself, don't leave it lying around,
clean it up now!

114
00:07:30,513 --> 00:07:31,138
I don't want to.

115
00:07:31,138 --> 00:07:32,264
It's really troublesome.

116
00:07:33,808 --> 00:07:37,620
Dry your hair, water droplets
from your hair are falling everywhere.

117
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:39,021
Let it be, it'll dry anyway.

118
00:07:39,021 --> 00:07:40,410
How long are you going to dry your hair?

119
00:07:40,410 --> 00:07:42,330
Put away your socks first,
you damn Young Lady.

120
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:44,910
The more you tell me, the more
I don't want to do it.

121
00:07:44,910 --> 00:07:46,195
Oh no.

122
00:07:46,195 --> 00:07:49,750
- Put it in the washing machine!
- A troublesome chemical reaction.

123
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:51,659
- It looks messy.
- Clean it up quickly, Young Lady!

124
00:07:51,659 --> 00:07:53,750
Enough, don't fight.

125
00:07:53,750 --> 00:07:55,496
Let's go eat first.

126
00:07:55,496 --> 00:07:57,998
I'm not eating,
I need to take care of my leg later.

127
00:07:57,998 --> 00:08:00,330
I want to watch videos.

128
00:08:00,330 --> 00:08:02,410
They only think about themselves.

129
00:08:02,410 --> 00:08:04,370
I'm going to eat.

130
00:08:04,370 --> 00:08:07,700
You guys better clean everything up
before we get back!

131
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:09,080
Okay.

132
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:22,140
Even though he's eating with me,

133
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:24,984
he hasn't said a single word.

134
00:08:27,410 --> 00:08:30,010
Is he still angry

135
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:32,200
about what I said to him
during the match?

136
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,034
Loser.

137
00:08:35,750 --> 00:08:37,500
Even though I was too fired up back then,

138
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:39,909
that word was really too harsh.

139
00:08:39,909 --> 00:08:41,000
Isagi.

140
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:41,751
Yes.

141
00:08:41,751 --> 00:08:46,830
Well, I want to ask you something.

142
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:50,410
What do you see on the field?

143
00:08:50,410 --> 00:08:53,596
What kind of soccer do you want to play?

144
00:08:55,870 --> 00:08:57,250
That...

145
00:08:57,250 --> 00:09:01,290
my skill is spatial cognition
and direct shooting,

146
00:09:01,290 --> 00:09:04,607
combined with free attacking positioning.

147
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:09,910
Doesn't this mean you can
dominate the field?

148
00:09:09,910 --> 00:09:11,370
Tell me from the start.

149
00:09:11,370 --> 00:09:13,407
Uh, I've told you before.

150
00:09:13,407 --> 00:09:16,450
Even though it was to win the match,

151
00:09:16,450 --> 00:09:18,662
what I said was really too harsh.

152
00:09:19,790 --> 00:09:22,000
Although I'd like you to take back
that word "loser,"

153
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,200
I don't think there's anything wrong
with your other statements.

154
00:09:25,044 --> 00:09:28,910
I just wasn't mature enough,
that's all.

155
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:30,700
I'm not a coward who refuses to change

156
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:32,384
even after experiencing suffering.

157
00:09:32,384 --> 00:09:36,096
I rose from the dead,
and I'm still very strong.

158
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:40,351
What's with this guy? So cool.

159
00:09:40,351 --> 00:09:42,620
Anyway, hurry up and tell me,

160
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:45,790
what kind of style do you want
this soccer team to play?

161
00:09:45,790 --> 00:09:47,580
Thank you, Barou.

162
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:51,487
I think I quite like
the current you.

163
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:55,407
I still hate you.

164
00:09:55,407 --> 00:09:59,330
Besides, I intend to devour your talent
by understanding you better,

165
00:09:59,330 --> 00:10:02,160
and make you accept defeat.

166
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:04,230
You're thanking an antagonist like me.

167
00:10:04,230 --> 00:10:06,669
Seems like the protagonist will be replaced soon.

168
00:10:06,669 --> 00:10:08,580
Fine, just try it.

169
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:10,540
I'll tell you
everything about myself,

170
00:10:10,540 --> 00:10:13,884
then evolve twice as fast as you.

171
00:10:13,884 --> 00:10:15,540
How naive.

172
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:18,450
I'll evolve three times faster.

173
00:10:18,450 --> 00:10:21,000
I won't just devour you,

174
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,660
but all of them as well.

175
00:10:25,437 --> 00:10:27,898
Is this my shirt?

176
00:10:27,898 --> 00:10:29,450
I don't know.

177
00:10:30,580 --> 00:10:32,111
What have you been watching?

178
00:10:32,111 --> 00:10:34,040
Super play videos.

179
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:35,906
This guy's play

180
00:10:35,906 --> 00:10:37,870
is great for stopping practice,

181
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:39,120
I want to imitate it.

182
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:42,288
Uh, that's Noel Noa.

183
00:10:42,288 --> 00:10:43,497
Who's he?

184
00:10:43,497 --> 00:10:46,120
The current number one striker in the world.

185
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,950
Ah, no wonder.

186
00:10:47,950 --> 00:10:49,753
This guy's soccer technique is really amazing.

187
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:55,290
Seriously? You really
don't understand soccer,

188
00:10:55,290 --> 00:10:58,290
but can play so well.
It's completely absurd.

189
00:10:58,290 --> 00:10:59,250
Thanks for the compliment.

190
00:10:59,805 --> 00:11:03,750
Oh yeah, has your leg ever been injured?

191
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:05,290
You said you were going to take care of your leg.

192
00:11:05,290 --> 00:11:07,910
Yeah, something like that.

193
00:11:07,910 --> 00:11:12,830
My right leg could be considered a time bomb,
and it's also my best partner.

194
00:11:13,950 --> 00:11:14,830
Does it hurt?

195
00:11:14,830 --> 00:11:16,370
It doesn't hurt anymore now,

196
00:11:16,370 --> 00:11:19,370
but it'll be bad if it gets injured again.

197
00:11:19,370 --> 00:11:21,000
Even so, I don't regret it.

198
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,830
I was mentally prepared
before I kept running every day.

199
00:11:26,330 --> 00:11:27,791
So cool.

200
00:11:27,791 --> 00:11:29,770
Before becoming number one in the world,

201
00:11:29,770 --> 00:11:32,950
there are many people who have to be defeated.

202
00:11:32,950 --> 00:11:34,000
Oh, yeah, Nagi.

203
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,450
Actually, there's another player whose
stopping technique is really amazing too.

204
00:11:36,450 --> 00:11:38,969
Really? Tell me quickly.

205
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:45,309
For us, there are many more
possibilities after this.

206
00:11:45,309 --> 00:11:47,311
The changed Barou,

207
00:11:47,311 --> 00:11:49,410
plus Nagi, Chigiri, and me.

208
00:11:49,410 --> 00:11:51,500
What kind of soccer can we play?

209
00:11:52,450 --> 00:11:56,080
I really can't wait
to play a match with them soon.

210
00:11:58,790 --> 00:12:00,866
They should have cleaned everything up,
right?

211
00:12:01,742 --> 00:12:04,453
Why is it messier than before?

212
00:12:06,330 --> 00:12:08,040
He even did it with shoes.

213
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:10,580
What are you doing?

214
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:13,370
I wanted to try it after watching the video.

215
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:15,881
Seishiro Nagi can turn anything
into a stopping selection stage.

216
00:12:16,757 --> 00:12:18,968
Besides, those are my shoes!

217
00:12:18,968 --> 00:12:19,950
Does Barou want to try too?

218
00:12:19,950 --> 00:12:23,830
- Bachira, Rin, wait.
- He can't do it.

219
00:12:23,830 --> 00:12:26,450
Right now, we're following
the enthusiasm in our hearts

220
00:12:26,450 --> 00:12:28,435
and accepting the challenge before us.

221
00:12:28,435 --> 00:12:30,896
And, we will win!

222
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:34,540
Start, once again.

223
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:38,112
Not bad, Rin.

224
00:12:38,112 --> 00:12:40,698
Isn't it time to bring out
your real ability?

225
00:12:40,698 --> 00:12:43,659
Shut up, Kappa Head,
you're too boring.

226
00:12:43,659 --> 00:12:47,290
But after playing ball with me,
you seem happier, right?

227
00:12:47,290 --> 00:12:51,834
Dribbling that relies on feelings
is useless to me.

228
00:12:51,834 --> 00:12:54,545
How can you know if you haven't tried?

229
00:12:54,545 --> 00:12:56,040
I do know.

230
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:59,290
When you dribble,
you look very happy.

231
00:12:59,290 --> 00:13:02,080
But actually, you're very afraid
of kicking the ball alone.

232
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:04,304
You play soccer
to chase a certain figure.

233
00:13:05,597 --> 00:13:10,330
Such a boring individualist
cannot excite me.

234
00:13:13,063 --> 00:13:18,027
(Blue Lock)

235
00:13:22,870 --> 00:13:27,540
Meguru Bachira, loves soccer balls very much.

236
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:30,790
Whether sleeping or awake,
from morning till night,

237
00:13:30,790 --> 00:13:34,540
he truly can't be separated from it.

238
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:37,290
Besides that,
he really loves dribbling.

239
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:40,080
Sometimes, he feels...

240
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,717
Like he can do it.

241
00:13:41,717 --> 00:13:46,750
The feeling of becoming one with soccer
is a very enjoyable sensation!

242
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:49,180
"In this world, there is nothing"

243
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:52,040
"more fun than this."

244
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:53,979
That is Meguru's belief.

245
00:13:53,979 --> 00:13:55,410
Bang!

246
00:13:56,774 --> 00:13:58,410
So boring.

247
00:13:58,410 --> 00:14:00,319
Come on, let's go home and play games.

248
00:14:00,319 --> 00:14:02,029
Why?

249
00:14:02,029 --> 00:14:04,700
What matters is that everyone
becomes one with soccer.

250
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:07,040
That way, you can play
really amazing soccer.

251
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:09,578
There's nothing more fun than soccer.

252
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:13,330
That sounds really creepy.

253
00:14:13,330 --> 00:14:14,540
You're just a Kappa Head.

254
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:16,877
Come on, let's go! This guy is too weird.

255
00:14:17,878 --> 00:14:19,379
I'm not weird!

256
00:14:19,379 --> 00:14:21,006
So disgusting!

257
00:14:21,006 --> 00:14:22,716
I'm not weird!

258
00:14:23,950 --> 00:14:25,450
So noisy!

259
00:14:27,660 --> 00:14:29,700
You're not weird at all.

260
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:31,250
Yes, Mom.

261
00:14:31,250 --> 00:14:33,910
They must be wrong.

262
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:36,660
But they're not wrong either.

263
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:38,760
It's just that the sense
that only you can feel,

264
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:40,984
they can't feel it.

265
00:14:40,984 --> 00:14:43,290
Then, what should I do?

266
00:14:43,290 --> 00:14:46,290
I just want to play soccer
with everyone else.

267
00:14:46,290 --> 00:14:48,540
Playing soccer is more fun
than playing games.

268
00:14:49,950 --> 00:14:51,453
Meguru is really great.

269
00:14:51,453 --> 00:14:55,500
Sticking to what you believe in
is a really great thing.

270
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:57,417
You just need to live
believing in your stance.

271
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:00,670
When you grow up,

272
00:15:00,670 --> 00:15:04,000
everyone will not dare
to believe in what they want to believe.

273
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,385
So, they can only
pretend not to see.

274
00:15:06,385 --> 00:15:10,120
Over time, they can no longer
hear the voice in their hearts clearly.

275
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:12,430
While what you believe in is

276
00:15:12,430 --> 00:15:15,660
an important thing that is so imaginative.

277
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:23,944
Even if it's the voice of a "monster"
inside your heart,

278
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:28,031
Mom still believes in that voice.

279
00:15:29,250 --> 00:15:31,830
The joy that only I can feel.

280
00:15:31,830 --> 00:15:34,746
So I can believe in this feeling
and keep playing soccer.

281
00:15:34,746 --> 00:15:36,039
Start, yeah, one more ball.

282
00:15:39,330 --> 00:15:41,044
After that,

283
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,370
Meguru started playing soccer
with the "monster."

284
00:15:51,096 --> 00:15:53,015
The spirit of "one team."

285
00:15:53,015 --> 00:15:55,950
Everyone must fight for victory.

286
00:15:55,950 --> 00:15:56,540
Alright!

287
00:15:56,540 --> 00:15:59,146
- The sky is so blue, so beautiful.
- One team!

288
00:16:00,731 --> 00:16:01,940
Bachira, pass the ball!

289
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:04,120
If I pass there, it won't be fun.

290
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:06,410
I want to pass two or three steps
ahead of that spot.

291
00:16:06,910 --> 00:16:08,447
If it was the "monster,"

292
00:16:08,447 --> 00:16:10,830
he could definitely shoot and score
with super amazing ball technique.

293
00:16:11,533 --> 00:16:12,951
Too high, I can't get it.

294
00:16:12,951 --> 00:16:15,662
Bachira, shouldn't that ball have been
passed right to the feet?

295
00:16:15,662 --> 00:16:18,123
Yeah.

296
00:16:18,660 --> 00:16:20,830
So the sun isn't red,

297
00:16:20,830 --> 00:16:23,040
it's white.

298
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:25,440
He believes there is definitely someone

299
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:28,250
who feels the same happiness as him.

300
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:31,290
He succeeded in scoring, Noel Noa!

301
00:16:31,290 --> 00:16:34,859
The strikers in the video,

302
00:16:34,859 --> 00:16:37,370
they all kicked the ball like a "monster."

303
00:16:37,370 --> 00:16:40,250
He wished that one day
he could play soccer like that.

304
00:16:41,230 --> 00:16:42,250
(National High School Soccer Selection Tournament)
One day

305
00:16:42,250 --> 00:16:43,600
(Chiba Prefecture Final Match)
he could meet someone

306
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:46,235
who can feel this joy in his heart.

307
00:16:46,235 --> 00:16:46,985
Bachira!

308
00:16:46,985 --> 00:16:48,830
So slow.

309
00:16:53,951 --> 00:16:56,787
With an ability like this,
you won't be able to defeat the monster.

310
00:16:57,913 --> 00:16:59,910
What are you doing?
You held onto the ball too long.

311
00:16:59,910 --> 00:17:02,580
Can you stop playing by yourself?

312
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:05,349
When he realized it, it was
the voice of the monster that was ignored

313
00:17:05,349 --> 00:17:08,410
and could not be heard by anyone.

314
00:17:08,410 --> 00:17:12,869
One day, the fun of soccer
was no longer cared about by anyone

315
00:17:12,869 --> 00:17:15,450
and Meguru could only keep moving forward.

316
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:17,974
But...

317
00:17:19,935 --> 00:17:23,689
sometimes he does feel scared.

318
00:17:23,689 --> 00:17:27,200
If you change that ambiguous technique,
you could become a professional athlete.

319
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,580
Shouldn't you have passed at that time?

320
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:30,570
Can you pass the ball
while looking at us properly?

321
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:35,556
If this continues,
there will be no one who understands.

322
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:41,330
If this continues,
playing soccer alone...

323
00:17:42,250 --> 00:17:45,580
Am I weird?

324
00:17:48,410 --> 00:17:50,380
Once he remembers this,

325
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:53,750
Meguru immediately feels
a loneliness that strikes like death.

326
00:17:56,513 --> 00:17:58,750
Meguru, are you home?

327
00:17:58,750 --> 00:17:59,599
What's wrong?

328
00:17:59,599 --> 00:18:02,978
Nothing, just feeling a little tired.

329
00:18:04,540 --> 00:18:06,064
There's a letter for you.

330
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:10,250
(Mr. Meguru Bachira, You Have Been Selected
as a Special Training Candidate)

331
00:18:11,695 --> 00:18:14,330
That's great, go!

332
00:18:14,330 --> 00:18:16,250
Are you happier now?

333
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:25,751
Noel Noa.

334
00:18:25,751 --> 00:18:26,960
Ronaldo.

335
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:28,950
Messi.

336
00:18:28,950 --> 00:18:30,172
Chico.

337
00:18:30,172 --> 00:18:32,660
Chico, pass the ball.

338
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:39,348
Pass the ball, Chico.

339
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:43,450
The person hit by the ball
becomes it.

340
00:18:43,450 --> 00:18:45,896
When time runs out,
the person who is still it

341
00:18:45,896 --> 00:18:47,856
is the one who gets locked off.

342
00:18:47,856 --> 00:18:51,080
Also, using hands is prohibited.

343
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:53,330
Is this soccer?

344
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:58,540
This kid is still sleeping.

345
00:18:58,540 --> 00:18:59,743
Got you.

346
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:07,209
This is a foul.

347
00:19:07,209 --> 00:19:08,580
In a match, you'd get a red card for this.

348
00:19:08,580 --> 00:19:12,120
He only said using hands is prohibited, didn't he?

349
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,540
Morning!

350
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:16,500
I hate dirty play.

351
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:18,470
Play fair.

352
00:19:18,470 --> 00:19:21,200
Are you a serious honor student?

353
00:19:22,641 --> 00:19:23,700
(Rensuke Kunigami)

354
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,352
In Blue Lock,

355
00:19:25,352 --> 00:19:27,854
there must be many soccer players.

356
00:19:27,854 --> 00:19:31,410
There must be someone who can match the monster.

357
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:39,408
- Damn it. Get off!
- Good chance.

358
00:19:39,408 --> 00:19:42,250
This is a place where serious soccer is played.

359
00:19:42,250 --> 00:19:43,870
For him, it was truly heaven.

360
00:19:44,913 --> 00:19:46,164
It hurts so much.

361
00:19:46,164 --> 00:19:47,290
Move away quickly.

362
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:53,410
Oh no, stop!

363
00:19:54,172 --> 00:19:57,410
Isagi! Now! Kick it quickly.

364
00:19:57,410 --> 00:19:58,750
If

365
00:19:58,750 --> 00:20:02,806
there's no one here who
can match the monster,

366
00:20:02,806 --> 00:20:05,830
then there will be no one who understands.

367
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:07,580
That's not true.

368
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:11,660
If it continues like this,
this is no different from my old self.

369
00:20:11,660 --> 00:20:13,870
I came to change my life.

370
00:20:13,870 --> 00:20:16,153
I came to become number one in the world.

371
00:20:17,779 --> 00:20:19,910
You're not bad.

372
00:20:19,910 --> 00:20:21,660
At that moment, I'll return again

373
00:20:21,660 --> 00:20:26,621
to those lonely days like death.

374
00:20:26,621 --> 00:20:29,700
Right. If you want to defeat an opponent,

375
00:20:30,709 --> 00:20:33,830
of course you have to choose the strongest.

376
00:20:33,830 --> 00:20:34,870
No.

377
00:20:36,590 --> 00:20:38,410
I don't want to be lonely anymore.

378
00:20:39,217 --> 00:20:41,428
So, even if I have to be scared,

379
00:20:41,428 --> 00:20:44,620
even if I have to be sad if I don't find it.

380
00:20:45,432 --> 00:20:48,370
Alright. There.

381
00:20:48,370 --> 00:20:50,540
I kept waiting.

382
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:54,500
Kept searching for the monster I could meet.

383
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:57,777
If it's a friend, it must be there.

384
00:20:58,620 --> 00:21:00,290
I found it.

385
00:21:00,290 --> 00:21:03,200
You have to choose the strongest kid.

386
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:03,950
Bang!

387
00:21:06,910 --> 00:21:10,120
It seems, Meguru heard that voice.

388
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,666
"Pass the ball."

389
00:21:11,666 --> 00:21:13,830
"He is a monster."

390
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:20,540
Therefore, Meguru
truly believes in Yoichi Isagi.

391
00:21:24,250 --> 00:21:25,830
Since that moment,

392
00:21:25,830 --> 00:21:29,000
I'm sure the person who can
fully understand my soccer,

393
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:33,563
who can feel the same joy,
is only Yoichi Isagi.

394
00:21:34,750 --> 00:21:37,484
This thought hasn't changed until now.

395
00:21:37,484 --> 00:21:38,700
But...

396
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:41,540
When you dribble,
you look very happy for a moment,

397
00:21:41,540 --> 00:21:43,700
but actually, you're very afraid
of kicking alone.

398
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:46,034
Actually, you kick
to chase a certain target.

399
00:21:47,250 --> 00:21:51,830
How could Rin know
that I'm chasing a certain target?

400
00:21:52,540 --> 00:21:55,870
It's the first time someone
has said that to me.

401
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:01,160
He's the only one who
notices the monster inside my heart.

402
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:03,718
I keep a monster in my heart.

403
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:06,137
What is it?

404
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:11,000
Like a soccer figure inside my heart.

405
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:14,896
I came to Blue Lock
to find the real monster.

406
00:22:14,896 --> 00:22:16,580
Who knows?

407
00:22:16,580 --> 00:22:20,000
If you're controlled by
something so childish like that,

408
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,700
then your playing technique
is very uninteresting.

409
00:22:23,700 --> 00:22:27,040
Play soccer with that monster
for your whole life.

410
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:30,950
At that time, I will
become number one in the world.

411
00:22:30,950 --> 00:22:36,910
Maybe for me, he is
a monster I still can't understand.

412
00:22:36,910 --> 00:22:39,546
A monster different from Isagi.

413
00:22:45,302 --> 00:22:48,221
Bachira, I've been looking for you.

414
00:22:48,221 --> 00:22:50,223
Isagi.

415
00:22:51,474 --> 00:22:54,936
As promised, I came
to take you back.

416
00:22:54,936 --> 00:22:59,399
Then, Meguru decided to fight
to confirm his thoughts.

417
00:23:00,580 --> 00:23:03,450
Let's have a match, Rin.

418
00:23:03,987 --> 00:23:07,080
Yoichi Isagi and Rin Itoshi.

419
00:23:07,080 --> 00:23:11,330
Which monster can make

420
00:23:11,330 --> 00:23:13,290
his mood even more excited?

421
00:23:14,450 --> 00:23:18,000
Blue Lock Extra Scene!

422
00:23:18,620 --> 00:23:21,338
(#19 The Late Team)
Looks like we have to form a team to pass.

423
00:23:21,338 --> 00:23:22,290
(Akuhito Iemon)
Alright.

424
00:23:22,290 --> 00:23:24,970
After all,
Kuon once betrayed us

425
00:23:24,970 --> 00:23:26,718
and no one wants
to be on the same team as him.

426
00:23:26,718 --> 00:23:29,080
(Wataru Kuon)
Sorry.

427
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:32,265
Actually, it's okay
if you leave me.

428
00:23:32,265 --> 00:23:33,870
(Yudai Imamura)
No, it's fine.

429
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:37,790
Iemon and I are slow to pass the stages,
we're the late team.

430
00:23:37,790 --> 00:23:39,039
Rather than being picky

431
00:23:39,039 --> 00:23:41,700
and getting eliminated
because we can't form a team,

432
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:43,430
it's better to quickly form a team
with someone we know,

433
00:23:43,430 --> 00:23:45,653
that's the best way.

434
00:23:45,653 --> 00:23:47,850
(Kuon, Imamura, Iemon Form a Team)
But, if you betray us again,

435
00:23:47,850 --> 00:23:49,250
(Pointing)
you'll be punished by death.

436
00:23:49,250 --> 00:23:50,870
No. If I really betray again,

437
00:23:50,870 --> 00:23:53,200
please just kill me.

438
00:23:53,830 --> 00:23:56,790
Finally...

439
00:23:57,582 --> 00:24:02,580
finally I can play
in a position other than goalkeeper.

440
00:24:02,580 --> 00:24:04,500
Come to think of it,
after coming this far,

441
00:24:04,500 --> 00:24:08,370
I haven't done any
striker-related movements either.

442
00:24:08,370 --> 00:24:11,410
Times like this are so long.

443
00:24:11,410 --> 00:24:14,450
But the boring days
will soon be over.

444
00:24:14,450 --> 00:24:16,976
Finally, I can take
my first step as a striker.

445
00:24:16,976 --> 00:24:18,870
Iemon, you keep being the goalkeeper.

446
00:24:18,870 --> 00:24:21,022
No!

447
00:24:22,290 --> 00:24:24,450
- Just kidding.
- I don't want... goalkeeper...

448
00:24:24,450 --> 00:24:27,570
Sorry, but you don't need to cry.

449
00:24:27,570 --> 00:24:29,540
- Hey!
- Staff!

450
00:24:29,540 --> 00:24:33,580
(The Three of Them Got Even More Late
Because Iemon Fainted)